# Block32 preexecution five-physicist panel return

This is an author-side portfolio challenge, not review-loop or an audit
verdict.

| lens | verdict |
|---|---|
| measurement foundations | use the complete local pointer projectors and keep the persistent selector distinct from a framework Record |
| reversible computation | a closed finite unitary cannot implement `Ready -> Spent` while fixing the same Spent state; retain a channel environment/history debit |
| locality / QCA | the complete NN validator is feasible but expensive; test the law-selective factor-level transaction before compiling it |
| stochastic processes | conjugate the guarded channel by `U` and require exact prefix consistency and second-application identity |
| gravity / portfolio | additive one-tip sources are `lambda`-blind; solve the transaction locus first, then send any surviving fork to a pair-sensitive source bridge |

The constructive panel found a bounded one-use NN validator/control lift with
roughly thousands of logical gates, but an independent portfolio challenge
ranked it below the symbolic guarded transaction: a green validator is likely
to be necessary plumbing and has little chance to select `lambda`.  The panel
therefore selected a `C -> B` hybrid: first build the persistent state-carrier
CPTP channel and solve its exact `lambda` locus; only then decide which local
Stinespring or validator component deserves compilation.

The strongest counterroute remains a pair-correlator-to-conserved-source law.
It is deliberately not prejudged here.
